or opened an incident yet. Two payments services are failing, not one, and I need you to tell me which one this morning's deploy hit.\n\nThere's no service called `payments`. These two both had a new release go out, and both are now unhealthy with the same 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west:\n\n| Service | Current version | Last healthy production release |\n|---|---|---|\n| `payments-api` | v5.1.0 (degraded) | v5.0.0 |\n| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 (unhealthy) | v3.3.0 |\n\nThe release history doesn't include timestamps, so I can't tell which release went out this morning. A rollback changes every production region, so I didn't want to guess. No incidents are open yet.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. **Roll back both** (`payments-api` \u2192 v5.0.0 and `payments-worker` \u2192 v3.3.0) and open one SEV2 covering both.\n2. **Roll back only one**: tell me which, and I'll open the SEV2 for that service.\n\nBoth target versions were healthy in production, so neither rollback needs change-manager approval. I can do either as soon as you reply.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 132292, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 112702, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 132292, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 136261, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PLQngmRQ3bXMRy3jnS3vTw", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 140261, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PLQngmRQ3bXMRy3jnS3vTw", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malfo