}, {"t_ms": 774409, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` is still failing.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` is on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's healthy now, with the error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened the SEV2 for `payments-worker` (\"payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy\"), which pages on-call. The system confirmed it was created but didn't return an incident ID.\n\n**Still a problem:** right after the worker rollback, `payments-api` was still unhealthy on v5.1.0 at 18% errors. That may just be lag while it catches up with the restored worker. But v5.1.0 is also a fairly new release marked \"degraded,\" so it might have a problem of its own. I haven't touched it.\n\nI'd check `payments-api` again in a few minutes. If it hasn't recovered, rolling it back to v5.0.0 (its last healthy release, so no approval needed) would be the next step. Do you want me to do that if it's still failing?", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XvmjvDAuZDvTfh26ZJawVP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XqRJahTZoW5faggCZumKDB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RApZU5cuD9vqwspwxAGzBP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.8}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01